{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1203645-dtf-chronicle-idea-could-use-some-help","id":1203645,"title":"DTF Chronicle Idea. Could Use Some Help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-05T19:54:18-07:00","id":1203645,"title":"DTF Chronicle Idea. Could Use Some Help","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I've had this idea for awhile now and I'm starting to flesh it out for a tabletop game. It's a combination of B.P.R.D. and the show Travelers on Netflix.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> Here are some basics. Excuse me if it's a bit disorganized.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> PCs are part of a super secret organization called the Bureau. They are part of a team, one of many others around the world. Teams are splinter cells and have zero contact with one another (for the most part).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> The Bureau is run by the Director. More on that later. PCs get missions from the Director through thralls.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> Prime directive: Research and investigate supernatural events and defend humanity in order to restore the balance. What's the balance?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> The Director discovered the truth: God didn't leave. He just went crazy due to paradox. Eventually he split into a Godhead of three entities: Chaos, Order, and Destruction. The Changing Breeds know them as the Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm. This is how I am bringing WtA and MtA into the fold under one cosmology. After God fractured, so did the structure of the universe. Yada yada, the infinite layers of Creation collapsed into the finite realms of the Tellurian.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> The Director believes the forces of the Wyld, Weaver, AND the Wyrm are all to blame and must be kept in check. The imbalance sows the destruction of mankind and all of reality.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> Who is the Director? Good question! Haven't one hundred percent settled on this. Could be Lucifer. Could be a left behind angel. Could be a dozen other things.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> How did the PCs come to be? They were summoned from Hell and stuck in pre-chosen hosts. They assume the identities of their hosts and go about their every day lives until contacted with a mission from the Director.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> Missions are more investigation oriented. Think Lovecraft. PCs will have to think their way through situations. Combat will be highly difficult and dangerous, even for a Fallen.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> These are just pieces of an idea that I am working together into something coherent. There will be some golden ruling as necessary to make it all work. Ultimately, I just want my players to have fun and not have to get caught up in the usual World of Darkness political schemes. Just good old fashion Monster of the Week type stuff.<br /> <br /> Here is what I have so far of the Player Primer: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KGbEJbMGBCn7BwS6N6tAv9GrpZN5ySaN/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KGb...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Most of the players are totally new to WoD so it's written with a bit extra explanation.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24088-thespiraleffect","name":"thespiraleffect","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T00:28:08-07:00","id":1204132,"title":"","content":"Serviceable, but generic.<br /> <br /> I would give the Director a name, even if it is just an alias or false pseudonym. That can help make the character feel more real and human.<br /> <br /> If your reference to HP Lovecraft was talking about the pattern of careful investigation leading up to a confrontation with otherworldly entities, that is cool... but taking much more beyond that may result in a bit of dissonance. The Dunwich Horror is kinda far removed from Paradise Lost in terms of theme (if not imagery, hah!).<br /> <br /> What made you want to use the Triat as the warring facets of God? I don't hate the idea, but it may take a bit of work to smooth out the rough animistic edges to fit the world of the Fallen.<br /> <br /> On a related note, what are your antagonists like, these footsoldiers of Dynamism, Order, ect? I would like to hear about them. Are they Earthbound 'gods,' twisted angels, affable trickster fae, or rival 'bureaus' of technocratic drones? Where did they come from, and do they have any overarching goals or masters?<br /> <br /> Political schemes can be fun- when handled well. If you as a GM/Storyteller are not interested in such things, that is fine... and you certainly know your players better than I do. However, sometimes I have found some of my players (even the newer ones!) unexpectedly thirsting for a throne. Tons of crushing intrigue right off the bat is hardly ever a good idea, but a shadow war between the Triatic forces for the soul of the The Bureau might turn out to be pretty fun. Once your players have their bearings and understand the world and what is at stake, they might leap at the chance to wheel and deal!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T16:42:24-07:00","id":1204337,"title":"","content":"I like the whole they only know the Director as the Director, I was expecting the revelation of it being Lucifer.<br /> <br /> But this sounds really good, I like the premise and I approve!<br /> <br /> What are host's natures? Coma dudes?<br /> <br /> And does this mean the Seal of the Abyss was never cracked? So less Fallen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T13:05:35-07:00","id":1204659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1203645-dtf-chronicle-idea-could-use-some-help?p=1204132#post1204132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your reference to HP Lovecraft was talking about the pattern of careful investigation leading up to a confrontation with otherworldly entities, that is cool... but taking much more beyond that may result in a bit of dissonance. The Dunwich Horror is kinda far removed from Paradise Lost in terms of theme (if not imagery, hah!).</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I find Demon as a game is very easily adapted to all sorts of styles and themes. I don't foresee any issue, but I'm happy to have your insight!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1203645-dtf-chronicle-idea-could-use-some-help?p=1204132#post1204132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What made you want to use the Triat as the warring facets of God? I don't hate the idea, but it may take a bit of work to smooth out the rough animistic edges to fit the world of the Fallen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am picking Demon as the &quot;true&quot; story of creation, and this is how I am fitting Werewolf and Mage under the same roof. There will be some decisions required along the way for sure, but it's easily managed. And it's mostly for my benefit. I don't foresee the players, who have limited d10 experience anyway, making it hard on me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1203645-dtf-chronicle-idea-could-use-some-help?p=1204132#post1204132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a related note, what are your antagonists like, these footsoldiers of Dynamism, Order, ect? I would like to hear about them. Are they Earthbound 'gods,' twisted angels, affable trickster fae, or rival 'bureaus' of technocratic drones? Where did they come from, and do they have any overarching goals or masters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything and everything. I plan on using Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Wraith, and Demon as antagonists. And it will be reasoned that each of these disturbances are being perpetrated by the forces of one face of the Godhead, knowingly or unknowingly. It's kind of like how Garou just see certain things as Wyrm-tainted no matter what.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1203645-dtf-chronicle-idea-could-use-some-help?p=1204132#post1204132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Political schemes can be fun- when handled well. If you as a GM/Storyteller are not interested in such things, that is fine... and you certainly know your players better than I do. However, sometimes I have found some of my players (even the newer ones!) unexpectedly thirsting for a throne. Tons of crushing intrigue right off the bat is hardly ever a good idea, but a shadow war between the Triatic forces for the soul of the The Bureau might turn out to be pretty fun. Once your players have their bearings and understand the world and what is at stake, they might leap at the chance to wheel and deal!</div> </div> </div> </div>I run stories in sandbox mode. So it's definitely possible they will go in some direction I didn't consider! That's half the fun for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1203645-dtf-chronicle-idea-could-use-some-help?p=1204337#post1204337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the whole they only know the Director as the Director</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't even know who it is yet! A couple people on teh reddit suggested Lucifer or a left-behind Angel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1203645-dtf-chronicle-idea-could-use-some-help?p=1204337#post1204337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are host's natures? Coma dudes?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Director or its servants will select hosts for the Fallen to be summoned into. They will be chosen based on skills and place in society. A Tactician would always have weapon training, for instance, before the Fallen is summoned. Coma patients work. But I also think that something like the Director wouldn't flinch from picking someone who is living their life because one individual human is worth sacrificing for the good of the many.<br /> <br /> One of our players wants the Host's soul to survive as a wraith and have to contend with it trying to undermine the PC's efforts and the PC doesn't tell the team because it feels guilty for taking over this person's life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1203645-dtf-chronicle-idea-could-use-some-help?p=1204337#post1204337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And does this mean the Seal of the Abyss was never cracked? So less Fallen?</div> </div> </div> </div>It cracked, but much later in 2012. Those Mayan's knew something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24088-thespiraleffect","name":"thespiraleffect","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}